{"availability":"available","full":"itsleeds/UK2GTFS","name":"UK2GTFS","description":"Convert UK transport data (TransXchange / ATOC CIF) to GTFS format in R","category":"Other","language":"R","stars":57,"forks":13,"created":"2019-02-20T16:11:12Z","updated":"2026-10-07T21:31:56Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://itsleeds.github.io/UK2GTFS/","topics":["atoc","bus","cif","data","gtfs","metro","r","train","tram","transport","transxchange","uk"],"demo":"https://itsleeds.github.io/UK2GTFS/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:42:16.584Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T09:42:16.584Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T09:42:16.584Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:42:16.584Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T08:58:19.164Z","stars":57,"forks":13},{"at":"2026-10-12T09:42:16.584Z","stars":57,"forks":13}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["UK2GTFS is an R package to convert and work with train, tram, bus, ferry, and metro timetable data from the unfriendly and difficult to use formats used in the UK to the easy to use GTFS format. The main purpose of developing the package is to support using OpenTripPlanner in the UK.","Example results are published as GitHub releases these come with no guarantee of quality.","The UK has two main sources of public transport timetable data Traveline publishes data on buses and light rail and National Rail publishes data on heavy rail. Each uses a data format that is unique to that organisation and both formats are old and difficult to use. Many countries have adopted the GTFS format which was developed by Google as a simple standard for publishing timetable data. Due to the wide-spread adoption of GTFS many useful tools have been developed that accept GTFS files as inputs. This package is intended to make the conversion of UK data to the GTFS format simple and easy."],"features":["(shapes.txt) built by routing services over a map of the UK rail network (atoc2gtfs(shapes = TRUE)) fares for buses, and the National Rail fares feed for heavy rail some parts which are not required for GTFS conversion…","Data cleaning, the raw data often contains clear errors, the package","heavy rail network that are on-demand)","GTFS tools, functions for working with GTFS data","gtfsfasttrips()) and columns, duplicated ids, referential integrity, enum and date/time values, and time/calendar logic across the whole feed including shapes, frequencies, transfers and fare tables and merging…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/itsleeds/UK2GTFS/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"fabd6876c7835054ccaab21f17d55013501325a51a16d3847ebeac30a2913fc9","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T08:58:19.164Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:42:16.584Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"UK2GTFS is an R package to convert and work with train, tram, bus, ferry, and metro timetable data from the unfriendly and difficult to use formats used in the UK to the easy to use GTFS format. The main purpose of developing the package is to support using OpenTripPlanner in the UK.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/itsleeds/UK2GTFS/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"fabd6876c7835054ccaab21f17d55013501325a51a16d3847ebeac30a2913fc9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/itsleeds/UK2GTFS/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T09:42:16.584Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T21:31:56Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/itsleeds/UK2GTFS/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T09:42:16.584Z","hash":"fabd6876c7835054ccaab21f17d55013501325a51a16d3847ebeac30a2913fc9","originalBytes":5243,"storedBytes":5243,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["gtfs","data","package","conversion","rail","bus","fares","shapes","transxchange","files","heavy","remotes","services","support","uk2gtfs","cif","cleaning","convert","errors","feed","format","github","including","national","subsetting